{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"callout","kind":"important","title":"Important","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This integration automates SSR dehydration/hydration and streaming between TanStack Router and TanStack Query. If you haven't read the standard "},{"type":"link","href":"../guide/external-data-loading.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"External Data Loading"}]},{"type":"text","value":" guide, start there."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-you-get","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What you get"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic SSR dehydration/hydration"}]},{"type":"text","value":" of your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming of queries"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that resolve during initial server render to the client"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Redirect handling"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redirect()"},{"type":"text","value":" thrown from queries/mutations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provider wrapping"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClientProvider"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The TanStack query integration is a separate package that you need to install:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/react-router-ssr-query\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/solid-router-ssr-query\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create your router and wire up the integration. Ensure a fresh "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" is created per request in SSR environments."}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { QueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration } from '@tanstack/react-router-ssr-query'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nexport function getRouter() {\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient()\n  const router = createRouter({\n    routeTree,\n    // optionally expose the QueryClient via router context\n    context: { queryClient },\n    scrollRestoration: true,\n    defaultPreload: 'intent',\n  })\n\n  setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration({\n    router,\n    queryClient,\n    // optional:\n    // handleRedirects: true,\n    // wrapQueryClient: true,\n  })\n\n  return router\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/router.tsx\"","title":"src/router.tsx","file":"src/router.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/router.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { QueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\nimport { setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration } from '@tanstack/react-router-ssr-query'\\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\\n\\nexport function getRouter() {\\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient()\\n  const router = createRouter({\\n    routeTree,\\n    // optionally expose the QueryClient via router context\\n    context: { queryClient },\\n    scrollRestoration: true,\\n    defaultPreload: 'intent',\\n  })\\n\\n  setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration({\\n    router,\\n    queryClient,\\n    // optional:\\n    // handleRedirects: true,\\n    // wrapQueryClient: true,\\n  })\\n\\n  return router\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the integration wraps your router with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClientProvider"},{"type":"text","value":". If you already provide your own provider, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wrapQueryClient: false"},{"type":"text","value":" and keep your custom wrapper."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dehydrateOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hydrateOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" to customize how TanStack Query serializes SSR payloads and restores them on the client."}]},{"type":"code","value":"setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration({\n  router,\n  queryClient,\n  dehydrateOptions: {\n    shouldDehydrateQuery: (query) => query.meta?.ssr !== false,\n  },\n  hydrateOptions: {\n    defaultOptions: {\n      queries: {\n        gcTime: 60_000,\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common uses for these options:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hydrateOptions.defaultOptions.queries.gcTime"},{"type":"text","value":" to control how long hydrated SSR queries stay in the client cache before garbage collection."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dehydrateOptions.shouldDehydrateQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" to exclude queries you do not want serialized into the HTML payload."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dehydrateOptions.serializeData"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hydrateOptions.defaultOptions.deserializeData"},{"type":"text","value":" when your SSR payload needs custom serialization."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { QueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration } from '@tanstack/react-router-ssr-query'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nexport function getRouter() {\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\n  const router = createRouter({\n    routeTree,\n    context: { queryClient },\n  })\n\n  setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration({\n    router,\n    queryClient,\n    hydrateOptions: {\n      defaultOptions: {\n        queries: {\n          gcTime: 5 * 60 * 1000,\n        },\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  return router\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/router.tsx\"","title":"src/router.tsx","file":"src/router.tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ssr-behavior-and-streaming","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR behavior and streaming"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"During server render, the integration dehydrates initial queries and streams any subsequent queries that resolve while rendering."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the client, the integration hydrates the initial state, then incrementally hydrates streamed queries."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queries from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSuspenseQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" or loader prefetches participate in SSR/streaming. Plain "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" does not execute on the server."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"use-in-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use in routes"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-usesuspensequery-vs-usequery","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using useSuspenseQuery vs useQuery"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSuspenseQuery"},{"type":"text","value":": runs on the server during SSR when its data is required and will be streamed to the client as it resolves."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":": does not execute on the server; it will fetch on the client after hydration. Use this for data that is not required for SSR."}]}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Suspense: executes on server and streams\nconst { data } = useSuspenseQuery(postsQuery)\n\n// Non-suspense: executes only on client\nconst { data, isLoading } = useQuery(postsQuery)","lang":"tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"// Suspense: executes on server and streams\\nconst { data } = useSuspenseQuery(postsQuery)\\n\\n// Non-suspense: executes only on client\\nconst { data, isLoading } = useQuery(postsQuery)\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"preload-with-a-loader-and-read-with-a-hook","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preload with a loader and read with a hook"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preload critical data in the route "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" to avoid waterfalls and loading flashes, then read it in the component. The integration ensures server-fetched data is dehydrated and streamed to the client during SSR."}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"blocking query in loader"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { queryOptions, useSuspenseQuery, useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst postsQuery = queryOptions({\n  queryKey: ['posts'],\n  queryFn: () => fetch('/api/posts').then((r) => r.json()),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  // Ensure the data is in the cache before render\n  loader: ({ context }) =>\n    context.queryClient.query({\n      ...postsQuery,\n      // returns data from cache immediately, otherwise executes a fetch\n      staleTime: 'static',\n    }),\n  component: PostsPage,\n})\n\nfunction PostsPage() {\n  // Prefer suspense for best SSR + streaming behavior\n  const { data } = useSuspenseQuery(postsQuery)\n  return <div>{data.map((p: any) => p.title).join(', ')}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"blocking query in loader\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"blocking query in loader\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { queryOptions, useSuspenseQuery, useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query'\\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\nconst postsQuery = queryOptions({\\n  queryKey: ['posts'],\\n  queryFn: () => fetch('/api/posts').then((r) => r.json()),\\n})\\n\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\\n  // Ensure the data is in the cache before render\\n  loader: ({ context }) =>\\n    context.queryClient.query({\\n      ...postsQuery,\\n      // returns data from cache immediately, otherwise executes a fetch\\n      staleTime: 'static',\\n    }),\\n  component: PostsPage,\\n})\\n\\nfunction PostsPage() {\\n  // Prefer suspense for best SSR + streaming behavior\\n  const { data } = useSuspenseQuery(postsQuery)\\n  return <div>{data.map((p: any) => p.title).join(', ')}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"prefetching-and-streaming","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefetching and streaming"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also prefetch with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query"},{"type":"text","value":" in a loader without consuming the data in a component. If you return the promise directly from the loader, it will be awaited and thus block the SSR request until the query finishes. If you don't await the promise nor return it, the query will be started on the server and will be streamed to the client without blocking the SSR request."}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"non-blocking query in loader"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { noop, queryOptions, useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query'\n\nconst userQuery = (id: string) =>\n  queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['user', id],\n    queryFn: () => fetch(`/api/users/${id}`).then((r) => r.json()),\n  })\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/user/$id')({\n  loader: ({ context, params }) => {\n    // Do not await this nor return the promise, just kick off the query to stream it to the client\n    void context.queryClient.query(userQuery(params.id)).catch(noop)\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/users.$id.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/users.$id.tsx","file":"src/routes/users.$id.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"non-blocking query in loader\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"non-blocking query in loader\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/users.$id.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\nimport { noop, queryOptions, useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query'\\n\\nconst userQuery = (id: string) =>\\n  queryOptions({\\n    queryKey: ['user', id],\\n    queryFn: () => fetch(`/api/users/${id}`).then((r) => r.json()),\\n  })\\n\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/user/$id')({\\n  loader: ({ context, params }) => {\\n    // Do not await this nor return the promise, just kick off the query to stream it to the client\\n    void context.queryClient.query(userQuery(params.id)).catch(noop)\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Previous versions of this guide used "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryClient.ensureQueryData"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryClient.prefetchQuery"},{"type":"text","value":". These methods are now deprecated in TanStack Query in favor of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryClient.query"},{"type":"text","value":". See the TanStack Query "},{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/query/latest/docs/framework/react/guides/migrating-to-v5#imperative-queryclient-methods","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v5 migration guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for more details."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"redirect-handling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Redirect handling"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a query or mutation throws a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redirect(...)"},{"type":"text","value":", the integration intercepts it on the client and performs a router navigation."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enabled by default"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disable with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handleRedirects: false"},{"type":"text","value":" if you need custom handling"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"works-with-tanstack-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Works with TanStack Start"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start uses TanStack Router under the hood. The same setup applies, and the integration will stream query results during SSR automatically."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"what-you-get","text":"What you get","level":2},{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"setup","text":"Setup","level":2},{"id":"ssr-behavior-and-streaming","text":"SSR behavior and streaming","level":2},{"id":"use-in-routes","text":"Use in routes","level":2},{"id":"using-usesuspensequery-vs-usequery","text":"Using useSuspenseQuery vs useQuery","level":3},{"id":"preload-with-a-loader-and-read-with-a-hook","text":"Preload with a loader and read with a hook","level":3},{"id":"prefetching-and-streaming","text":"Prefetching and streaming","level":3},{"id":"redirect-handling","text":"Redirect handling","level":2},{"id":"works-with-tanstack-start","text":"Works with TanStack Start","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","solid"],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> This integration automates SSR dehydration/hydration and streaming between TanStack Router and TanStack Query. If you haven't read the standard [External Data Loading](../guide/external-data-loading.md) guide, start there.\n\n## What you get\n\n- **Automatic SSR dehydration/hydration** of your `QueryClient`\n- **Streaming of queries** that resolve during initial server render to the client\n- **Redirect handling** for `redirect()` thrown from queries/mutations\n- Optional **provider wrapping** with `QueryClientProvider`\n\n## Installation\n\nThe TanStack query integration is a separate package that you need to install:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/react-router-ssr-query\nsolid: @tanstack/solid-router-ssr-query\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Setup\n\nCreate your router and wire up the integration. Ensure a fresh `QueryClient` is created per request in SSR environments.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/router.tsx\"\nimport { QueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration } from '@tanstack/react-router-ssr-query'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nexport function getRouter() {\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient()\n  const router = createRouter({\n    routeTree,\n    // optionally expose the QueryClient via router context\n    context: { queryClient },\n    scrollRestoration: true,\n    defaultPreload: 'intent',\n  })\n\n  setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration({\n    router,\n    queryClient,\n    // optional:\n    // handleRedirects: true,\n    // wrapQueryClient: true,\n  })\n\n  return router\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nBy default, the integration wraps your router with a `QueryClientProvider`. If you already provide your own provider, pass `wrapQueryClient: false` and keep your custom wrapper.\n\nYou can also pass `dehydrateOptions` and `hydrateOptions` to customize how TanStack Query serializes SSR payloads and restores them on the client.\n\n```tsx\nsetupRouterSsrQueryIntegration({\n  router,\n  queryClient,\n  dehydrateOptions: {\n    shouldDehydrateQuery: (query) => query.meta?.ssr !== false,\n  },\n  hydrateOptions: {\n    defaultOptions: {\n      queries: {\n        gcTime: 60_000,\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nCommon uses for these options:\n\n- Set `hydrateOptions.defaultOptions.queries.gcTime` to control how long hydrated SSR queries stay in the client cache before garbage collection.\n- Set `dehydrateOptions.shouldDehydrateQuery` to exclude queries you do not want serialized into the HTML payload.\n- Set `dehydrateOptions.serializeData` and `hydrateOptions.defaultOptions.deserializeData` when your SSR payload needs custom serialization.\n\n```tsx title=\"src/router.tsx\"\nimport { QueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration } from '@tanstack/react-router-ssr-query'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nexport function getRouter() {\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\n  const router = createRouter({\n    routeTree,\n    context: { queryClient },\n  })\n\n  setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration({\n    router,\n    queryClient,\n    hydrateOptions: {\n      defaultOptions: {\n        queries: {\n          gcTime: 5 * 60 * 1000,\n        },\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  return router\n}\n```\n\n## SSR behavior and streaming\n\n- During server render, the integration dehydrates initial queries and streams any subsequent queries that resolve while rendering.\n- On the client, the integration hydrates the initial state, then incrementally hydrates streamed queries.\n- Queries from `useSuspenseQuery` or loader prefetches participate in SSR/streaming. Plain `useQuery` does not execute on the server.\n\n## Use in routes\n\n### Using useSuspenseQuery vs useQuery\n\n- `useSuspenseQuery`: runs on the server during SSR when its data is required and will be streamed to the client as it resolves.\n- `useQuery`: does not execute on the server; it will fetch on the client after hydration. Use this for data that is not required for SSR.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\n// Suspense: executes on server and streams\nconst { data } = useSuspenseQuery(postsQuery)\n\n// Non-suspense: executes only on client\nconst { data, isLoading } = useQuery(postsQuery)\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Preload with a loader and read with a hook\n\nPreload critical data in the route `loader` to avoid waterfalls and loading flashes, then read it in the component. The integration ensures server-fetched data is dehydrated and streamed to the client during SSR.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# Blocking `query` in loader\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.tsx\"\nimport { queryOptions, useSuspenseQuery, useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst postsQuery = queryOptions({\n  queryKey: ['posts'],\n  queryFn: () => fetch('/api/posts').then((r) => r.json()),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  // Ensure the data is in the cache before render\n  loader: ({ context }) =>\n    context.queryClient.query({\n      ...postsQuery,\n      // returns data from cache immediately, otherwise executes a fetch\n      staleTime: 'static',\n    }),\n  component: PostsPage,\n})\n\nfunction PostsPage() {\n  // Prefer suspense for best SSR + streaming behavior\n  const { data } = useSuspenseQuery(postsQuery)\n  return <div>{data.map((p: any) => p.title).join(', ')}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Prefetching and streaming\n\nYou can also prefetch with `query` in a loader without consuming the data in a component. If you return the promise directly from the loader, it will be awaited and thus block the SSR request until the query finishes. If you don't await the promise nor return it, the query will be started on the server and will be streamed to the client without blocking the SSR request.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# Non-blocking `query` in loader\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/users.$id.tsx\"\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { noop, queryOptions, useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query'\n\nconst userQuery = (id: string) =>\n  queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['user', id],\n    queryFn: () => fetch(`/api/users/${id}`).then((r) => r.json()),\n  })\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/user/$id')({\n  loader: ({ context, params }) => {\n    // Do not await this nor return the promise, just kick off the query to stream it to the client\n    void context.queryClient.query(userQuery(params.id)).catch(noop)\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Previous versions of this guide used `queryClient.ensureQueryData` and `queryClient.prefetchQuery`. These methods are now deprecated in TanStack Query in favor of `queryClient.query`. See the TanStack Query [v5 migration guide](https://tanstack.com/query/latest/docs/framework/react/guides/migrating-to-v5#imperative-queryclient-methods) for more details.\n\n## Redirect handling\n\nIf a query or mutation throws a `redirect(...)`, the integration intercepts it on the client and performs a router navigation.\n\n- Enabled by default\n- Disable with `handleRedirects: false` if you need custom handling\n\n## Works with TanStack Start\n\nTanStack Start uses TanStack Router under the hood. The same setup applies, and the integration will stream query results during SSR automatically.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: query\ntitle: TanStack Query Integration\n---\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> This integration automates SSR dehydration/hydration and streaming between TanStack Router and TanStack Query. If you haven't read the standard [External Data Loading](../guide/external-data-loading.md) guide, start there.\n\n## What you get\n\n- **Automatic SSR dehydration/hydration** of your `QueryClient`\n- **Streaming of queries** that resolve during initial server render to the client\n- **Redirect handling** for `redirect()` thrown from queries/mutations\n- Optional **provider wrapping** with `QueryClientProvider`\n\n## Installation\n\nThe TanStack query integration is a separate package that you need to install:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/react-router-ssr-query\nsolid: @tanstack/solid-router-ssr-query\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Setup\n\nCreate your router and wire up the integration. Ensure a fresh `QueryClient` is created per request in SSR environments.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/router.tsx\"\nimport { QueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration } from '@tanstack/react-router-ssr-query'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nexport function getRouter() {\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient()\n  const router = createRouter({\n    routeTree,\n    // optionally expose the QueryClient via router context\n    context: { queryClient },\n    scrollRestoration: true,\n    defaultPreload: 'intent',\n  })\n\n  setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration({\n    router,\n    queryClient,\n    // optional:\n    // handleRedirects: true,\n    // wrapQueryClient: true,\n  })\n\n  return router\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nBy default, the integration wraps your router with a `QueryClientProvider`. If you already provide your own provider, pass `wrapQueryClient: false` and keep your custom wrapper.\n\nYou can also pass `dehydrateOptions` and `hydrateOptions` to customize how TanStack Query serializes SSR payloads and restores them on the client.\n\n```tsx\nsetupRouterSsrQueryIntegration({\n  router,\n  queryClient,\n  dehydrateOptions: {\n    shouldDehydrateQuery: (query) => query.meta?.ssr !== false,\n  },\n  hydrateOptions: {\n    defaultOptions: {\n      queries: {\n        gcTime: 60_000,\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nCommon uses for these options:\n\n- Set `hydrateOptions.defaultOptions.queries.gcTime` to control how long hydrated SSR queries stay in the client cache before garbage collection.\n- Set `dehydrateOptions.shouldDehydrateQuery` to exclude queries you do not want serialized into the HTML payload.\n- Set `dehydrateOptions.serializeData` and `hydrateOptions.defaultOptions.deserializeData` when your SSR payload needs custom serialization.\n\n```tsx title=\"src/router.tsx\"\nimport { QueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration } from '@tanstack/react-router-ssr-query'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nexport function getRouter() {\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\n  const router = createRouter({\n    routeTree,\n    context: { queryClient },\n  })\n\n  setupRouterSsrQueryIntegration({\n    router,\n    queryClient,\n    hydrateOptions: {\n      defaultOptions: {\n        queries: {\n          gcTime: 5 * 60 * 1000,\n        },\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  return router\n}\n```\n\n## SSR behavior and streaming\n\n- During server render, the integration dehydrates initial queries and streams any subsequent queries that resolve while rendering.\n- On the client, the integration hydrates the initial state, then incrementally hydrates streamed queries.\n- Queries from `useSuspenseQuery` or loader prefetches participate in SSR/streaming. Plain `useQuery` does not execute on the server.\n\n## Use in routes\n\n### Using useSuspenseQuery vs useQuery\n\n- `useSuspenseQuery`: runs on the server during SSR when its data is required and will be streamed to the client as it resolves.\n- `useQuery`: does not execute on the server; it will fetch on the client after hydration. Use this for data that is not required for SSR.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\n// Suspense: executes on server and streams\nconst { data } = useSuspenseQuery(postsQuery)\n\n// Non-suspense: executes only on client\nconst { data, isLoading } = useQuery(postsQuery)\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Preload with a loader and read with a hook\n\nPreload critical data in the route `loader` to avoid waterfalls and loading flashes, then read it in the component. The integration ensures server-fetched data is dehydrated and streamed to the client during SSR.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# Blocking `query` in loader\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.tsx\"\nimport { queryOptions, useSuspenseQuery, useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst postsQuery = queryOptions({\n  queryKey: ['posts'],\n  queryFn: () => fetch('/api/posts').then((r) => r.json()),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  // Ensure the data is in the cache before render\n  loader: ({ context }) =>\n    context.queryClient.query({\n      ...postsQuery,\n      // returns data from cache immediately, otherwise executes a fetch\n      staleTime: 'static',\n    }),\n  component: PostsPage,\n})\n\nfunction PostsPage() {\n  // Prefer suspense for best SSR + streaming behavior\n  const { data } = useSuspenseQuery(postsQuery)\n  return <div>{data.map((p: any) => p.title).join(', ')}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Prefetching and streaming\n\nYou can also prefetch with `query` in a loader without consuming the data in a component. If you return the promise directly from the loader, it will be awaited and thus block the SSR request until the query finishes. If you don't await the promise nor return it, the query will be started on the server and will be streamed to the client without blocking the SSR request.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# Non-blocking `query` in loader\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/users.$id.tsx\"\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { noop, queryOptions, useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query'\n\nconst userQuery = (id: string) =>\n  queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['user', id],\n    queryFn: () => fetch(`/api/users/${id}`).then((r) => r.json()),\n  })\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/user/$id')({\n  loader: ({ context, params }) => {\n    // Do not await this nor return the promise, just kick off the query to stream it to the client\n    void context.queryClient.query(userQuery(params.id)).catch(noop)\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Previous versions of this guide used `queryClient.ensureQueryData` and `queryClient.prefetchQuery`. These methods are now deprecated in TanStack Query in favor of `queryClient.query`. See the TanStack Query [v5 migration guide](https://tanstack.com/query/latest/docs/framework/react/guides/migrating-to-v5#imperative-queryclient-methods) for more details.\n\n## Redirect handling\n\nIf a query or mutation throws a `redirect(...)`, the integration intercepts it on the client and performs a router navigation.\n\n- Enabled by default\n- Disable with `handleRedirects: false` if you need custom handling\n\n## Works with TanStack Start\n\nTanStack Start uses TanStack Router under the hood. The same setup applies, and the integration will stream query results during SSR automatically.\n"}
